From 9db08e5fec0326fa7e2682ecf6a57925cc214d12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:56:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Air battle sound: riding a B-17 plays the real recording from
 inside one (Brian's Good, round seven)

Brian stamped round seven on the listening page at 21:40Z: b17_interior_loop
Good, plane_hit and hmg_burst_long Cut. Ridden, a B-17 now plays
b17_interior_loop open, at +2 dB (mix.json air.closeView.bed.interior,
interiorGainDb), in place of its drone through the 200 Hz filter: the same
loudness, measured (-18.0 against -18.2 LUFS). Its dead engines still dim it.
A model not listed, or the take not yet built into the game, keeps the
filtered drone. air.roundsHit stays silent (plane_hit Cut).

Sounds/Real: b17_interior_loop.wav (craigsmith, Freesound 437850, CC0), with
its credits row (Tools/make_credits.py).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L4rhz35oCkUv94Xb2EwCjp
